* ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
* PHOTONIC AI CHIP - TRANSIMPEDANCE AMPLIFIER SPICE SIMULATION
* ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
*
* Circuit: Single-channel TIA (Transimpedance Amplifier)
* Purpose: Validate circuit performance before PCB layout
* Simulation: NGSPICE or LTspice compatible
*
* Instructions for EDA Playground (www.edaplayground.com):
* 1. Go to: https://www.edaplayground.com
* 2. New project → NGSPICE
* 3. Copy this entire file into the editor
* 4. Click "Run" to simulate
* 5. Check waveforms in the "Simulation" tab
*
* ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

.title Photonic AI Chip - Transimpedance Amplifier Circuit

* ═════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
* CIRCUIT DESCRIPTION
* ═════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
*
* INPUT: Photodiode current source (Ge photodiode on PIC)
*   - Current range: 100 nA to 100 µA (depending on optical power)
*   - Capacitance: 50 pF (parallel)
*   - Dark current: 1 µA
*
* TIA CONFIGURATION:
*   - Op-Amp: OPA2356 (modeled as ideal voltage-controlled voltage source)
*   - Feedback resistor: 10 MΩ (transimpedance gain = 10 MV/A)
*   - Feedback capacitor: 50 pF (stability compensation)
*   - Open-loop gain: 100 dB
*   - GBW: 1.4 GHz
*
* OUTPUT: 0 to 3.3V single supply
*   - Swing: 0V (darkness) to 3.3V (bright light)
*   - Bandwidth: ~160 MHz (-3dB)
*   - Noise: ~4 pA/√Hz (dominated by op-amp input current noise)
*
* ═════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

* ═════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
* POWER SUPPLIES
* ═════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

VCC 1 0 DC 3.3V         * Single supply: +3.3V
VEE 2 0 DC 0V           * Ground reference

* ═════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
* INPUT SOURCE: Photodiode current
* ═════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

* Pulse of optical power (1 ns rise time, simulating optical pulse)
* Current source: 1 µA per 100 mW of optical power (example: 1% efficiency)
* Pulse: 0 to 10 µA in 1 ns, hold for 10 ns

IPD 3 0 PULSE(1u 10u 0ns 1ns 1ns 10ns 100ns)
*   Start, Stop, Delay, Rise, Fall, Width, Period

* Photodiode parasitic capacitance (parallel to current source)
CPD 3 0 50p

* ═════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
* TIA CIRCUIT: OPA2356 Transimpedance Amplifier
* ═════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

* Node assignment:
*   3 = Non-inverting input (from photodiode)
*   4 = Inverting input (feedback node)
*   5 = Op-amp output (internal)
*   6 = Final output (after compensation network)
*   1 = VCC (+3.3V)
*   2 = GND (0V)

* Feedback network (determines transimpedance):
*   Rf = 10 MΩ → Gain = 10 V/µA = 10 MV/A
*   Cf = 50 pF → Compensation for stability

RF 4 6 10MEG          * Feedback resistor: 10 MΩ
CF 4 6 50p            * Feedback capacitor: 50 pF

* Op-Amp Model (Ideal model - approximates OPA2356)
* Voltage-controlled voltage source with frequency response
* Open-loop gain: 100 dB (100,000 V/V)
* GBW: 1.4 GHz → cutoff at 1.4G / 100k = 14 kHz (closed-loop bandwidth ≈ GBW/Gain)

* Simple model using VCVS + frequency-dependent impedance
EAMP 5 2 3 4 100000    * VCVS: Gain = 100,000 (100 dB)
                       * Input diff: (3) - (4)
                       * Output: (5) to (2)

* Frequency compensation (1.4 GHz GBW)
* Dominant pole at ~14 kHz (closed-loop)
ROUT 5 6 1k            * Output impedance (high-freq damping)
COUT 6 2 100p          * Output capacitance

* Input bias current (OPA2356: Ib ≈ 1 pA)
IB 3 2 DC 1p           * 1 pA bias current

* ═════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
* COMPARATOR INPUT STAGE (Next stage - optional verification)
* ═════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

* Reference voltage: 1.65V (mid-rail, created by resistor divider)
VREF 10 0 DC 1.65V

* Comparator input impedance (high impedance, negligible load)
RIN 6 0 100k

* ═════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
* SIMULATION COMMANDS
* ═════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

* Transient simulation: 0 to 1 µs with 1 ns time steps
.tran 0 1u 0 1n

* .control section (for ngspice)
.control
run

* Print key measurements
echo "TIA Performance Summary"
echo "======================"
echo "Input current pulse: 1 µA to 10 µA step"
echo "Expected output:"
echo "  - DC gain: 10 MΩ → 10 mV per µA"
echo "  - Step 1 µA → 10 mV output"
echo "  - Step 10 µA → 100 mV output"
echo ""
echo "Transient analysis plots:"
echo "  1. Input current (IPD voltage across 50Ω dummy resistor)"
echo "  2. TIA output voltage (V6)"
echo "  3. Phase margin / stability check"
echo ""

* Calculate phase margin (advanced - requires Bode plot)
* Recommended: Plot V(6) and observe overshoot
*   - Good TIA: <10% overshoot
*   - Unstable TIA: oscillation or ringing > 20%

.endc

* ═════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
* PLOTTING INSTRUCTIONS (EDA Playground)
* ═════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
*
* After simulation completes:
*
* 1. Plot Input Current:
*    - Type: V(3) (node at photodiode input)
*    - Shows: Photodiode current pulse
*
* 2. Plot TIA Output:
*    - Type: V(6) (TIA output node)
*    - Expected: 0 to 100 mV step with possible ringing
*    - Good design: Rise time < 5 ns, overshoot < 10%
*
* 3. Phase & Magnitude (Bode Plot - if EDA supports):
*    - Sweep frequency from 1 MHz to 1 GHz
*    - Look for: -3dB point (bandwidth)
*    - Expected: ~160 MHz for this configuration
*
* ═════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
* EXPECTED SIMULATION RESULTS
* ═════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
*
* Transient Response (0-100 ns):
*   Time = 0 ns: IPD = 1 µA → V(6) = 10 mV
*   Time = 1 ns: IPD jumps to 10 µA (1 ns rise time)
*   Time = 1-2 ns: V(6) rises from 10 mV toward 100 mV
*   Time = 2 ns: V(6) should reach ~95 mV (5% overshoot acceptable)
*   Time = 11 ns: IPD returns to 1 µA
*   Time = 11-12 ns: V(6) falls back to 10 mV
*
* Stability Indicators:
*   ✓ Good: Smooth rise, minimal ringing, settling < 5 ns
*   ✗ Bad: Oscillation, ringing > ±20% of final value
*   ✗ Unstable: Divergent oscillation (unbounded)
*
* If oscillation observed:
*   → Increase Cf (feedback capacitor)
*   → Example: Try Cf = 100 pF, re-simulate
*   → Trade-off: Higher Cf → slower response, more stable
*   → For 10 MΩ Rf and 50 pF Cf: Dominant pole ≈ 318 Hz (very safe)
*
* ═════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
* NOISE ANALYSIS (Advanced - Optional)
* ═════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
*
* To analyze input-referred noise:
* 1. Replace transient pulse with:
*    IPD 3 0 DC 5u AC 1u    (5 µA DC + 1 µA AC for frequency sweep)
*
* 2. Add noise analysis commands:
*    .ac dec 100 1M 100G     (Decade sweep, 100 points/decade, 1M to 100G Hz)
*    .noise v(6) IPD        (Output-referred noise)
*
* 3. Expected noise floor: ~1 nV/√Hz (very low due to OPA2356)
*    - Photodiode shot noise: sqrt(2*q*Ipd) ≈ 18 pA/√Hz @ 5µA
*    - TIA input-referred noise: < 5 pA/√Hz
*    - Total RTI (referred-to-input): ~20 pA/√Hz
*
* ═════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
* COMPONENT VARIATIONS (Sensitivity Analysis)
* ═════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
*
* To test design robustness, modify component values and re-run:
*
* Test 1: Rf variations (temperature drift, tolerance)
*   RF 4 6 9MEG            (±10% variation: 9-11 MΩ)
*   Expected: Output scales proportionally (9-11 mV per µA input)
*
* Test 2: Cf variations (PCB parasitic capacitance)
*   CF 4 6 75p             (Worst-case: 50p + 25p parasitics)
*   Expected: Slightly slower response, better stability
*
* Test 3: Cpd variations (larger photodiode)
*   CPD 3 0 100p           (Larger Ge photodiode: 100 pF)
*   Expected: May need larger Cf for stability, slower bandwidth
*
* ═════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

.end

* ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
* END OF SIMULATION FILE
* ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
